    <section class="section section--cream-deep" id="principles">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section-head">
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow"><span class="roman">III.</span>&nbsp;House principles</p>
            <h2 class="display">Four rules.<br/><em>Nothing else.</em></h2>
          </div>
          <div class="sub-block">
            <p class="sub">
              The discipline that holds the channel together &mdash; written once at the founding,
              re-read every Monday before the TSX bell.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="principles">
          <article class="principle reveal">
            <div class="principle-num">I</div>
            <h3>One brief per trading day.</h3>
            <p>Sent at 7:30 AM Pacific. Nothing on weekends. Nothing on Canadian federal holidays. If the brief is late, the market closes for you.</p>
            <span class="tag">Cadence &middot; non-negotiable</span>
          </article>

          <article class="principle reveal">
            <div class="principle-num">II</div>
            <h3>Only Canadian-listed miners.</h3>
            <p>TSX, TSX-V and the CSE. Gold, silver, uranium, copper, lithium and high-conviction junior explorers. No U.S. equities. No crypto. No general market noise.</p>
            <span class="tag">Scope &middot; narrow on purpose</span>
          </article>

          <article class="principle reveal">
            <div class="principle-num">III</div>
            <h3>Thesis. Drill. Trigger. Stop.</h3>
            <p>Four lines, in that order. Resource-quality citation (g/t Au, % Cu, lbs U<sub>3</sub>O<sub>8</sub>) is mandatory. No 2,000-word teardown. No paid course at the end of the rainbow.</p>
            <span class="tag">Format &middot; under 200 words</span>
          </article>

          <article class="principle reveal">
            <div class="principle-num">IV</div>
            <h3>Membership is private.</h3>
            <p>WhatsApp Channel is broadcast-only. Other members cannot see your number, your name, or that you joined. Leave with one tap, anytime.</p>
            <span class="tag">Privacy &middot; broadcast only</span>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

