          <div class="copy">
            <p class="kicker">6:58 AM Pacific &middot; the morning ritual</p>
            <h4>Two cups in. <em>One brief out.</em></h4>
            <p>The day starts at six. Gold, silver, copper and uranium settle prints from the prior US session read first &mdash; LBMA AM fix, COMEX prompt-month, LME 3-month copper, SPUT spot uranium, USD/CAD.</p>
            <p>Then the TSX-V tape: drill results from SEDAR+, infill assays, NR releases, NI&nbsp;43-101 amendments. A 90-minute scan compresses into a 188-word WhatsApp note.</p>
            <p>By the time the open hits at 9:30 AM Eastern, the brief has been read at over nine thousand kitchen tables, prospector trucks and Bay Street trading desks.</p>
            <p class="signoff">&ldquo;Grade is king. Everything else is noise.&rdquo; &mdash; the desk&rsquo;s only painted-on rule.</p>
